From 1217c2e1065b8b12a261b2f74f3b53bd7cc6105d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JuanPZuluaga <juanz9312@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 1 Jun 2026 06:34:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] [Perf][Bugfix] voxtral_tts hot path: cudagraph opt-out,
 host-sync removal, kernel caches

Signed-off-by: JuanPZuluaga <juanz9312@gmail.com>

Local fork resolution (perso): decode_one_frame keeps the per-request
`noise` / `n_steps` overrides; the schedule cache is keyed on
(dtype, n_steps) instead of dtype alone so per-request euler steps are
cached too. Also pass `noise` in the new outer-capture fallback of the
CUDA-graph wrapper, which would otherwise drop a request's seed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
